git status
git checkout -b my-branch-name
git add .
git commit -m "Update project"
Push the branch to GitHub:

git push -u origin my-branch-name

After that, future pushes from the same branch can simply use:

git push

-------------------------
If the branch already exists locally:

git switch my-branch-name
git add .
git commit -m "Update project"
git push
--------------------------
If the branch exists on GitHub but not locally:

git fetch origin
git switch -c my-branch-name --track origin/my-branch-name

Then:

git add .
git commit -m "Update project"
git push

For example, if your branch is called portfolio-update:

git switch -c portfolio-update
git add .
git commit -m "Improve portfolio website"
git push -u origin portfolio-update

